course: dictionary
lesson: 8747
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things, and context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around it first. «Sesame seeds» on a bun are tiny seeds, but «Open sesame!» from a story is not about seeds at all.
explain: «Tāngyuán are sweet rice balls in warm syrup, often with black sesame inside.» Here sesame is food, the little black seeds inside the rice ball. The clues are sweet, warm syrup and inside. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: Some words are magic in stories. In «Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves», the words «Open sesame!» open the robbers' cave. People also say it as a joke when a door opens by itself, or when something gives you an easy way in.
fact: Sesame is a plant grown in warm countries for its small flat seeds.
fact: Sesame seeds are tiny, cream or black, and often sprinkled on bread, buns and bagels.
fact: Sesame seeds are pressed to make sesame oil, and they are used in foods like tahini and hummus.
fact: «Open sesame!» is the magic password in the story «Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves».
fact: On food labels, sesame is listed as an allergen, so read labels carefully if a friend is allergic.
exercise: «Tāngyuán are sweet rice balls in warm syrup, often with black sesame inside.» What is the sesame in this sentence? | A kind of warm syrup | The magic words that open a cave | *Tiny black seeds inside the rice balls | A plant with tall stems
exercise: Which story has the magic words «Open sesame!»? | Robin Hood | Peter Pan | *Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves | Cinderella
exercise: Why do food labels list sesame? | Because it is a country | *Because some people are allergic to it | To show it is a magic word | To make the food taste sweeter
test: Jokingly, someone says «Open sesame!» when a door opens by itself. What does the phrase mean here? | A password to a secret cave | *An easy way to get what you want | A bread roll with seeds | A plant that grows in the desert
test: What is sesame oil made from? | *Pressed sesame seeds | Pressed rice balls | Black pepper | Warm syrup
exam: Mia reads «The bagel had sesame on top» and thinks sesame is a magic word. What does sesame mean here? | *Tiny seeds sprinkled on top of the bagel | A plant with big flowers | A magic word that opens doors | A cave full of gold
